      "solution": {
        "status": "ambiguous",
        "reasoning": "The Jacobian is [[2-4x-y,-x],[4y,-2+4x]], giving [[-1,-0.5],[4,0]] at (0.5,1), consistent with MA's captured correct grades. Its characteristic polynomial is \\lambda^2+\\lambda+2, so the eigenvalues are -0.5\\pm0.5\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{i}. Their negative real parts and nonzero imaginary parts imply an asymptotically stable spiral sink. Although asymptotic stability also implies stability, 'an asymptotically stable' is the precise classification. MA evidence for fields 5–7 has not been captured.",
